1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:03,150
Teacher midterm practice, question 10.

2
00:00:03,770 --> 00:00:06,268
In Figure 1, what does point L indicate?

3
00:00:07,967 --> 00:00:10,776
F is fracture. Two lines drop from F.

4
00:00:10,776 --> 00:00:12,704
One goes straight down to M.

5
00:00:12,704 --> 00:00:16,505
The other is parallel to the elastic line, and lands at L.

6
00:00:17,126 --> 00:00:21,361
The parallel line is the elastic spring back when the specimen breaks.

7
00:00:21,361 --> 00:00:25,486
So L is the strain that remains: the plastic strain at fracture.

8
00:00:26,105 --> 00:00:29,349
M is the total strain at fracture, and the gap from

9
00:00:29,349 --> 00:00:32,475
L to M is the elastic part that was recovered.

10
00:00:34,075 --> 00:00:36,936
The answer is D: the plastic strain at fracture.

11
00:00:37,756 --> 00:00:40,319
The vertical drop gives the total strain.

12
00:00:40,319 --> 00:00:44,111
The line parallel to the elastic slope gives the plastic strain.
